From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spaced: lvm may check semaphore support

Gentoo's lvm2 (pvs, which spaced runs) checks SysV semaphore support with
semctl even with udev sync off; spaced's policy killed it. Google's policy
for os_install_service, which runs lvm too, allows it.

---
--- a/spaced/seccomp/spaced-seccomp-amd64.policy
+++ b/spaced/seccomp/spaced-seccomp-amd64.policy
@@ -76,6 +76,9 @@
 quotactl: 1
 read: 1
 readlink: 1
+# NickelOS Unified: Gentoo's lvm2 (pvs) checks SysV semaphore support first,
+# as Google's policy for os_install_service allows lvm.
+semctl: 1
 recvmsg: 1
 rename: 1
 restart_syscall: 1
